WEBVTT

00:21:29.538 --> 00:21:31.829
the record straight or learn from
something from this experience.

00:21:31.871 --> 00:21:35.746
And so you're almost inviting the leader
to be a problem solver as opposed to.

00:21:35.788 --> 00:21:37.163
Yes. Calling them the problem.

00:21:37.663 --> 00:21:39.496
That's right. And so it is.

00:21:39.496 --> 00:21:42.913
We have this list of kind of we you know,
we call hard conversations, rumbles.

00:21:43.329 --> 00:21:46.746
And in fact, I have one schedule today
and it literally says in my calendar,

00:21:47.163 --> 00:21:49.204
ad sales rumball four o'clock.

00:21:50.413 --> 00:21:53.204
And so what I know what that
means in our organization,

00:21:53.204 --> 00:21:57.079
our culture is we're expecting
a lot of different opinions.

00:21:57.121 --> 00:21:59.163
We're expecting a lot of
competing priorities.

00:21:59.163 --> 00:22:01.829
Bring up a point of view, bring
a lot of curiosity,